<http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T072> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "A physical object is an identifiable collection of matter, which may be constrained by an identifiable boundary, and may move as a unit by translation or rotation, in 3-dimensional space." .
<http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T072> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
